From 26fee195a92aea02bbf95bdf9db35f88277e71a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harry Askham <harryaskham@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 00:05:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] bd-fbf784: gitignore .cacophony/images/ so generation
 output_dir stops re-dirtying the canonical checkout
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

generation.yaml writes generated images to output_dir .cacophony/images (4
entries), which was NOT in .gitignore. Each generation pass (~3-6min) left
untracked files in the canonical daemon checkout, dirtying it and blocking ALL
cacophony direct reintegrations (the dirty-checkout preflight refuses) — the
bd-ef7ec0 incident. Add .cacophony/images/ next to the .cacophony/tmp/
runtime-state entry; pure generated artefacts, never committed.

Verified: git check-ignore .cacophony/images/test-gen.png echoes the path.
---
 .gitignore | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/.gitignore b/.gitignore
index 616681d84..98e255b8d 100644
--- a/.gitignore
+++ b/.gitignore
@@ -17,6 +17,12 @@ configs/*.yaml
 # Runtime state written by repo-owned daemon automation
 .cacophony/tmp/
 
+# Generated images written by the generation.yaml output_dir (.cacophony/images).
+# Pure generated artefacts, never committed; otherwise each generation pass
+# re-dirties the canonical daemon checkout and blocks ALL cacophony direct
+# reintegrations (bd-ef7ec0).
+.cacophony/images/
+
 # Session summary artifacts are published to the Cacophony state sidecar,
 # not tracked at the repository root.
 /summary/
-- 
2.53.0

